  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.1,
      "end_seconds": 6.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "Doctor, we're ready in room two, I've already taken the the observations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.25,
      "end_seconds": 12.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "so, good, thank you welcome, tell me what's brought you in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.03,
      "end_seconds": 21.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "Um, so... pain in my back and hips. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.76,
      "end_seconds": 25.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "what's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.48,
      "end_seconds": 30.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "For about two weeks, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.09,
      "end_seconds": 41.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "So, can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.06,
      "end_seconds": 57.31,
      "duration_seconds": 14.25,
      "text": "Only regular tablets, and it's not much. Maybe a seven out of ten on a bad day. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.97,
      "end_seconds": 60.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.27,
      "end_seconds": 83.07,
      "duration_seconds": 20.8,
      "text": "Constipation goes along with it, you know, most of the time. The Constipation? That's been for two weeks. Actually, about Constipation, severe, I'd say. I've also had being very tired, since last Tuesday. With being very tired, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.81,
      "end_seconds": 88.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "A few quick ones: bleeding or confusion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.98,
      "end_seconds": 94.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "oh, you know, I haven't had bleeding or confusion, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.09,
      "end_seconds": 100.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "I follow. A A few quick ones: shortness of breath or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.1,
      "end_seconds": 106.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "I haven't had shortness of breath or vomiting, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.71,
      "end_seconds": 110.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.07,
      "end_seconds": 114.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.28,
      "end_seconds": 118.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.65,
      "end_seconds": 124.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "okay, so no, that's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.04,
      "end_seconds": 144.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.81,
      "end_seconds": 150.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "erm, I have depression, for about a year"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.86,
      "end_seconds": 154.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "okay, go on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.18,
      "end_seconds": 162.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Okay, so I've had heart failure for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.63,
      "end_seconds": 165.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.89,
      "end_seconds": 174.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "Alright, depression and heart failure, that matches what I have here. Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.65,
      "end_seconds": 177.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.88,
      "end_seconds": 182.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.67,
      "end_seconds": 196.22,
      "duration_seconds": 11.55,
      "text": "I take escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for my mood. It's spironolactone, 25 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.64,
      "end_seconds": 210.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.78,
      "end_seconds": 228.1,
      "duration_seconds": 16.32,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I have about eight cigarettes in a day. I hardly move around during the day. I'm vegetarian and have been for years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 232.63,
      "end_seconds": 243.2,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier. Respiratory rate 16, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, temperature is 36.7 degrees. BP is 111 over 70, heart rate 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.24,
      "end_seconds": 244.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.68,
      "end_seconds": 251.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.93,
      "end_seconds": 266.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.01,
      "end_seconds": 270.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.31,
      "end_seconds": 286.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "your tummy is soft and you look comfortable and thin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.71,
      "end_seconds": 314.37,
      "duration_seconds": 22.66,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. So where does that leave us? I'd lean towards cancer pain needing better control. Another possibility is opioid-induced constipation. For this, senna, 15 milligrams, at night, long term. You take it by mouth. It's for opioid-induced constipation. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.12,
      "end_seconds": 320.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "mm, can I collect it it from my own pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.14,
      "end_seconds": 348.01,
      "duration_seconds": 26.87,
      "text": "For this, morphine sulfate modified-release, 20 milligrams, twice a day, long term. You take it by mouth. That should help with cancer pain. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Take the long-acting tablet regularly and the liquid for breakthrough pain. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.69,
      "end_seconds": 350.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.86,
      "end_seconds": 361.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "Let's review you in one week. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.14,
      "end_seconds": 368.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "erm, you know, no, that's all thanks a lot"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.31,
      "end_seconds": 372.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Right, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
